.TH AXON 1 "2026-10-12" "Axon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
axon \- manage NeurOS packages with libalpm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-Q
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PACKAGE ...]
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-S
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TARGET ...]
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-U
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR ARCHIVE ...
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-R
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR PACKAGE ...
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.I MAINTENANCE-OPERATION
.RI [ PACKAGE ...]
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-\-ui
.PP
.B axon \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Axon is a C frontend to libalpm for NeurOS. It queries installed packages and
cached repositories, prepares and approves package transactions, and provides
maintenance commands and an interactive terminal browser.
It targets pacman 7.1 and libalpm ABI 16.
.PP
Select one operation. Query modifiers apply to
.B \-Q
or
.BR \-S ;
short options may have different meanings for removals.
Queries use cached data and do not refresh repositories.
Output goes to standard output; diagnostics and approval prompts go to standard error.
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read PATH instead of /etc/pacman.conf. The form \-\-config=PATH is accepted.
RootDir and DBPath are configured in this file; command-line root/sysroot
overrides are not implemented.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage without loading configuration. The process identity check still applies.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing before targets that begin with a dash.
.SH QUERIES
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-query
List installed names and versions. Exact package arguments restrict the list;
omitting them selects all installed packages.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
Show package details with \-Q or \-S. Omitted names select all packages.
Repository names may be qualified as REPOSITORY/PACKAGE.
Missing requested packages fail the command while other targets are processed.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-search
With \-Q or \-S, search descriptions and names using libalpm regular expressions.
All supplied patterns must match; omitted patterns list all eligible packages.
Repository searches honor Usage=Search. Repository duplicates remain visible.
No matches is a successful empty result. Unreadable caches are errors.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
With \-Q, list installed paths for the selected packages or all installed packages.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-owns
With \-Q, find installed owners of the supplied paths. At least one path is required.
Parent paths are resolved while the final symlink retains its identity.
Bare executable names are not searched through PATH.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-groups
With \-Q, list installed group members. With \-S and no group arguments, list
group names; repeating the flag (\-Sgg) lists members. Named groups list members.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-foreign
With \-Q, select packages absent from configured repository databases.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-native
With \-Q, select packages present in configured repository databases.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-explicit
With \-Q, select explicitly installed packages.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-deps
With \-Q, select packages installed as dependencies.
.PP
Native/foreign and explicit/dependency filters may be combined, but opposing
filters cannot. File ownership cannot be combined with these filters.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-check
With \-Q, check installed-file presence. Repeat (\-Qkk) to compare recorded
mtree type, permissions, owner/group, size, modification time and symlink targets.
Omitted package names select all installed packages.
.TP
.B \-\-checksums
With \-Qkk, also verify recorded SHA-256 or MD5 checksums.
Missing metadata or checksum coverage is reported as an inspection error.
.PP
Modified backup configuration content is distinguished from damaged files;
configuration type, permission and ownership errors still fail inspection.
Diagnostics identify paths and packages and suggest recovery actions.
Inspection neither repairs files nor removes database locks.
.SH TRANSACTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sync
Without query modifiers, install repository packages or groups.
Targets may be qualified as REPOSITORY/NAME. All eligible group members are
expanded into the approval plan; a numeric group subset chooser is not provided.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-upgrade
Install local package archives. Despite its long option name, this operation
requires archive paths; use \-Su or \-Syu for a full system upgrade.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remove
Remove installed packages after dependency resolution and approval.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-refresh
With \-S, refresh repositories. Repeat to force refresh.
\-Sy refreshes only; \-Syu refreshes before preparing a full upgrade.
Refresh operations take no package targets. Refresh-plus-individual-install
combinations are rejected to avoid partial upgrades.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-sysupgrade
With \-S, prepare a full system upgrade. \-Su uses cached repositories;
\-Syu requires a successful refresh before preparation. Package targets are not accepted.
.TP
.B \-\-needed
With repository installs, local archives or full upgrades, skip already-current packages.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-downgrade
Permit a downgrade plan for installs or upgrades. Separate confirmation is still required.
.SS Removal modifiers
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-recursive
Remove dependencies no longer needed by other packages.
Repeat (\-Rss) to include explicitly installed dependencies.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cascade
Include packages that depend on the removal targets.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nosave
Omit backup-file preservation during removal.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unneeded
Keep targets required by other installed packages.
.SS Approval and failure handling
Mutations require root and explicit confirmation. Axon presents resolved changes,
versions, sizes and flags before committing. HoldPkg protection applies to all
resolved removals, including cascades and replacements. Protected removals and
downgrades require additional acknowledgment. Explicit ignored package/group
targets are rejected. Signature, architecture, dependency, conflict and lock
checks remain active. There is no \-\-noconfirm option.
.PP
Cancellation is cooperative. A running transfer or package operation may finish
before interruption takes effect. A failed refresh may update some caches;
a failed commit may leave package changes. Axon does not roll changes back.
Read-only destinations are checked before commit, but successful preflight
cannot guarantee subsequent writes will succeed.
.PP
Hook, scriptlet and helper errors reported by libalpm cause failure even if
libalpm reports commit success. Diagnostics include observed completed package
operations. Those counts do not guarantee all files or scriptlets succeeded.
Cleanup failures and incomplete diagnostics prevent a success report.
Never remove a database lock without establishing that no package manager owns it.
.SH MAINTENANCE
.TP
.B \-\-orphans
List unneeded packages installed as dependencies.
.TP
.BI \-\-depends " PACKAGE..."
Inspect installed dependency relationships.
.TP
.BI \-\-asexplicit " PACKAGE..."
Mark installed packages explicitly installed, after approval.
.TP
.BI \-\-asdeps " PACKAGE..."
Mark installed packages as dependencies, after approval.
.TP
.B \-\-clean-cache
Review cache removals under CleanMethod. Retained package identity is determined
from package metadata; unrelated cache files are not blindly deleted.
.TP
.B \-\-check-db
Check local/sync records, archive integrity, dependency/conflict consistency,
and database locks. Malformed and inaccessible records are reported.
This command does not initialize missing databases or perform repairs.
.SH TERMINAL BROWSER
.B \-\-ui
opens the package browser using the same backend policy and approval interfaces
as the CLI. The screen lists available keys for browsing, filtering, details,
installation/removal, upgrades and maintenance. Small terminals show a resize
message. Failed or declined mutations retain a nonzero final exit status even
if the user returns to browsing.
.PP
Externally supplied terminal control characters, invalid multibyte bytes and
bidi controls are escaped. Labels are clipped by display columns without
splitting valid UTF-8 characters. Colors use blue, purple and green.
A nonempty NO_COLOR disables colors. Redirected streams and TERM=dumb omit
colors and progress redraws. Progress shows the most recently updated transfer;
unknown totals leave the bar unfilled. Output failure is reported as failure.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Axon reads pacman-style options and repository sections, Include files,
$repo/$arch mirror substitutions, Usage and signature policies.
Relative Includes use the process working directory. List settings append;
the first scalar path or DownloadUser wins. Signature overrides inherit the
completed global policy and later tokens override individual settings.
.PP
Unknown or misplaced directives, invalid values, duplicate repositories,
missing Includes, Include cycles and resource-limit violations are errors.
Comments occupy whole lines; inline hash characters are literal. Values are
not shell commands and receive no quote, environment or tilde expansion.
This parser is stricter than pacman for some malformed configurations.
.PP
Backend setup honors cache/hook/GPG/log paths, architectures, IgnorePkg,
IgnoreGroup, NoUpgrade, NoExtract, UseSyslog, CheckSpace, ParallelDownloads,
DownloadUser, download timeout/sandbox settings, servers and cache servers.
HoldPkg and CleanMethod are enforced by the operation and maintenance layers.
NoProgressBar disables progress bars. VerbosePkgLists and ILoveCandy are parsed
but do not select alternate layouts. XferCommand is parsed but explicitly
rejected during backend setup, including for queries.
.PP
SigLevel, LocalFileSigLevel and RemoteFileSigLevel control verification using
GPGDir. Defaults require trusted package and database signatures.
Verification failures never cause an unsigned retry. DownloadUser must name an
existing account; Axon does not silently disable its sandbox. DisableSandbox,
DisableSandboxFilesystem and DisableSandboxSyscalls are explicit overrides.
.PP
Ordinary backend initialization may create database directories where permitted.
File and database inspection requires existing state and does not initialize it.
.SH PRIVILEGES
Queries require accessible configuration and databases but not root.
Refresh, transactions, reason changes and cache removal require root.
Axon does not request passwords or automatically elevate privileges.
.PP
Mismatched real/effective/saved user or group IDs and secure-execution launches
are rejected. Install Axon without setuid/setgid bits or file capabilities.
An administrator's launcher must start an ordinary root process for mutations.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a search with no matches.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, privilege, backend, transaction, inspection or output failure;
a missing requested package; or a declined/cancelled mutation.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid options, combinations or required arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.conf
Default configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/local/
Default installed-package database.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/sync/
Default cached repository databases.
.PP
RootDir changes default DBPath/LogFile. Explicit DBPath remains independent
of RootDir; configure both for an alternate root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
axon \-Q
axon \-Qi pacman glibc
axon \-Qs '^pacman$'
axon \-Ss '^pacman$'
axon \-Qo /usr/bin/pacman
axon \-Qkk \-\-checksums pacman
axon \-\-check-db
axon \-\-config /path/to/pacman.conf \-Q
sudo axon \-Syu
sudo axon \-S \-\-needed package
sudo axon \-U ./package.pkg.tar.zst
sudo axon \-Rs package
axon \-\-ui
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
Axon implements a subset of pacman's interface, not every option or identical
detail output. Inspection and failure handling do not provide transactional
rollback or automatic boot recovery. Disposable NeurOS installation, full-upgrade
and reboot-recovery validation is required before adopting Axon as the default
system package manager.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR libalpm (3)
